WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.668
I want to turn to

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.068
the new

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:04.304
classified documents that the FBI found

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.339
at the president's house in Delaware.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.807
It was a 13 hour search

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.042
that happened on Friday.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.643
It's just the latest

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.545
revelation of the president

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.813
having classified items

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.015
that he shouldn't have.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.950
You've been in Congress for 40 years.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.918
You've handled classified material

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:19.953
for a lot of those years,

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.054
probably most of them.

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:24.157
How concerned are you about this?

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.092
Well, I'm concerned.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.727
There's a standard that we follow

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.629
when it comes to members of Congress

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.765
and classified information.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.933
The door to my office is closed.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.001
The person who presents

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:35.902
the document to me

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:38.338
takes it out of a locked briefcase,

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.607
hands it to me, and watches as I read it

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:41.941
when I finish reading it.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:42.809
He takes it back

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.344
and puts it in the briefcase

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.512
and leaves the scene.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.246
I mean, that's

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.681
how carefully we review these documents.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.082
To think

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:52.652
that any of them ended up in boxes

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.055
in storage, one place to the other

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.523
is just unacceptable.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:58.058
But having said that,

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.559
let me make this point clear.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.327
Joe Biden has said from the start,

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.096
we are going to be totally transparent

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.230
about this.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.032
Let the chips fall where they may.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.635
I'm going to open my home voluntarily.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:09.836
To a search,

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:10.804
not the first search,

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:13.540
I'm sure, of his offices at home.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.775
He has shown total cooperation

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:16.409
in this effort.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.677
That is a sharp contrast

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.412
to President Trump.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.080
Well, I want to.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.815
Speaking of former President Trump,

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:22.682
I want to play something

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.284
that you said last year

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.352
about the classified documents found

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.088
at his Mar a Lago resort.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.324
It's an outrage.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:31.691
It is a

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.026
literal outrage

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:33.660
for the president

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.595
to take this important information

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:38.364
down to his home in Florida.

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.200
And then store it in a closet

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.234
with traffic.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.535
People back and forth in

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.271
his resort and golf course is an outrage.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.674
Is it also an outrage

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.075
for the current president

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:52.112
to have what appears to be multiple

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.446
classified documents

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.849
in multiple locations

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.718
At its heart, the issue is the same.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.353
Those documents should not have been

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.122
in the personal possession

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.224
of either Joe Biden or Donald Trump.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.159
But what happened and followed from

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.161
it is significantly different.

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:08.895
Donald Trump

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:10.430
defied those who knew

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.065
the documents were in place

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.901
and ultimately led to involuntarily

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:15.702
a court order

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:18.838
and a search of his Mar a Lago hotel

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.273
resort to find out

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:22.008
how many documents were there.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.143
Contrast that with Joe

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:23.743
Biden,

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.245
embarrassed by the situation

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.946
as he should have been He

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.149
he invited the government agencies

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.450
in to carefully

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.718
look through all the boxes

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.919
he had accumulated.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:35.054
It's a much different approach.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.190
It is outrageous that either occurred,

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.826
but the reaction by the former president

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:40.793
and the current president

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.395
could not be in sharp contrast.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:43.630
They are they are very different.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.831
No question about that.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.468
Having said that, you are a politician.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.370
You've been around for a while

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.037
and you understand

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.873
how these things play out.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.643
Do you fear that because of that,

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:59.245
the current president has kind of lost

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.914
a high ground on this notion

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.815
of classified information

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.951
being where it shouldn't be

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.554
Well, of course,

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:09.422
let's be honest about it.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.191
When that information is found,

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:15.328
it diminishes the stature of any person

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.030
who is in possession of it

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.165
because it's not supposed to happen,

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.233
whether it was

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.268
the fault of a staffer or turning.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.570
It makes no difference.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.138
The elected official bears

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.839
ultimate responsibility.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.141
And we have to worry

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.742
since this new group

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:30.977
that has taken over control

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:32.545
of the House of Representatives

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:33.446
has promised us

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.015
endless investigations confrontations,

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.984
impeachments and chaos.

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.152
What's going to happen?

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.620
I only have one word for those

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.821
who are dubious as to

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:42.822
whether that will happen.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.657
And the word is Benghazi.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.092
How long did we spend

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:46.726
going through

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.094
Benghazi hearings

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:49.062
in the Republican

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:50.763
controlled House in the past?

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.799
Now, imagine the mega Republicans

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.901
and what they're setting out to do.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.035
I'm sure that they're going

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:58.304
to have investigations

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.872
to our hearts delight.

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.141
I want to turn to the debt ceiling, sir.

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:03.376
The White House insists

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.577
they are not going to negotiate

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:05.411
with Republicans

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.380
who are demanding spending cuts

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.282
in exchange for raising the debt limit

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:11.351
so America doesn't default on its debt.

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:12.218
Do you think the

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:13.453
president should negotiate

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.590
No, absolutely not.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.158
Let's get to the bottom line here.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.060
Those who are posing for holy pictures

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.262
as budget balancers,

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.830
the mega Republicans

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.366
should note one important fact.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:29.969
Almost 25% of all of the national debt

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.671
accumulated over the history

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:32.905
of the United States.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.274
230 years

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.241
was accumulated

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.277
during the four years of Donald Trump.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.712
So the notion that there is some

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.114
partizan holy position

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.515
that they're taking

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:43.383
in, that they're going

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:44.617
to fight this battle

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.686
a matter of principle

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:48.521
when they enact the tax cuts

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.256
for the wealthiest people of America

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.824
during the Trump administration,

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:52.392
they added

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:54.327
dramatically to the national debt,

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:55.628
which we are now facing.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:56.863
Having done that,

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.631
they need to face the responsibility

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.832
of paying for it.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.968
That is what the debt limit is about.

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:04.237
And if we play games with this,

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:07.140
if we delay this, if we have short term

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.608
extensions of the national debt,

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.843
we run the very risk of a recession

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.011
in this economy.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.112
Millions of Americans

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:14.914
out of work and interest rates going

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:15.948
even higher.

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:16.683
Denying people

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:17.250
an opportunity

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:17.617
to buy

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.786
a home or car in this economy

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:20.953
will be stalled.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.322
We shouldn't play games

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.289
with the national debt.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.124
When Joe Biden was vice president.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.559
I'm sure you remember

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:27.894
back in 2011,

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:28.695
he was the lead

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:31.230
negotiator on negotiations

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:32.832
for spending cuts

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.867
in exchange for raising the debt ceiling.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:35.968
But you think you're saying

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:36.769
you think it's different

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:37.670
because of what happened

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:38.504
during the Trump years

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.641
I think it's different.

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:43.109
Not just because the Trump here

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:45.178
is being the origin of much of this debt

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:47.113
but by the new House of Representatives.

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:49.248
15 ballots down that you were there

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:49.982
you saw it

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.884
or at least witnessed on television

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:53.953
15 ballots to choose the speaker

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.122
and he gave the authority

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:58.191
to each member of the House

00:05:58.191 --> 00:05:59.525
to initiate a vote

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.661
of no confidence on a daily basis.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:02.729
I mean,

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:05.131
this is a House of Representatives which

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:07.500
is under control of the mega

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.369
Republicans at this point.

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:10.203
And I'm fearful

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.804
that very few constructive

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:12.872
things will emerge.

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:13.706
Before I let you go.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.708
I have to ask about the Supreme Court.

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:16.509
You are, of course,

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:17.810
Senate Judiciary chairman.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.712
You saw what happened at the court.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:20.680
They announced this week

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.647
that they were unable

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:22.281
to determine

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.951
who leaked the draft decision overturning

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:26.853
Roe versus Wade last year.

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:27.720
Clerks

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.857
and employees had to sign sworn affidavit

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:32.024
saying that they didn't leak

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:33.092
the draft opinion.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:35.128
The justices,

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:35.995
neither the justices

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:36.829
nor their spouses

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.865
actually had to sign affidavits

00:06:38.865 --> 00:06:40.900
So do you believe that

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:41.701
that was a mistake?

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:42.902
Should they have to do

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.904
so to figure out where the leak

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:45.371
came from?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.675
Listen, the universe of people

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:50.643
who are suspects

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:51.611
in this

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:53.880
leak of the opinion of the Supreme Court

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.748
is really a small universe.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:57.350
It includes the justices

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.117
and their families.

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:00.186
If they had access to this opinion,

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:02.088
which I assume some of them did.

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:04.524
They should have gone into the least

00:07:04.524 --> 00:07:05.825
the position of assertions

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:07.660
by each one of the justices

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:08.828
as to what they did

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:09.662
or did not do

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:11.531
when it came to these opinions.

00:07:11.531 --> 00:07:14.500
But I find it hard to imagine with this

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.502
small group of people who had access

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:17.804
to this opinion,

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:18.671
they couldn't come up

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:20.373
with more information.

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:22.074
Are you going to try, in your capacity

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:23.743
as judiciary chair

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:26.846
No, I don't think this is an area

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:29.882
where we can go in with any kind of force

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:33.052
and make four changes result

00:07:33.052 --> 00:07:33.853
at this point.

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:34.554
Okay.

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:35.788
Senate Judiciary Chairman

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:37.256
Dick Durbin, thank you so much.

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:39.459
And I should say the Senate whip.

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:40.960
Thank you so much for joining me

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.028
this morning. Appreciate it.

